      "math_academy_id": "q-183812",
      "problem": "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $Z∼N(0,1),$ compute $P(Z<2.22).$\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.02\\,$ | $\\,0.03\\,$ | $\\,0.04\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,-2.3\\,$ | $\\,0.0102\\,$ | $\\,0.0099\\,$ | $\\,0.0096\\,$ |\n| $\\,-2.2\\,$ | $\\,0.0132\\,$ | $\\,0.0129\\,$ | $\\,0.0125\\,$ |\n| $\\,-2.1\\,$ | $\\,0.0170\\,$ | $\\,0.0166\\,$ | $\\,0.0162\\,$ |",
